<main class="min-h-screen">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <%!--
      The showcase: a hero, then one <section> per theme in the order a visitor
      evaluates Stride (Plan, Build, Review, then Operate and Measure). Every
      screenshot comes from demo data and is listed, with how to retake it, in
      priv/static/images/marketing/README.md. test/kanban_web/controllers/marketing_images_test.exs
      checks each <img> exists under /images/marketing/ and declares its real size,
      and that every subsection marked data-showcase-item shows an image or a code
      snippet.
    --%>
    <header class="text-center mb-20">
      <span class="ucase">{gettext("Product")}</span>
      <h1
        class="font-semibold mt-3 mb-5"
        style="font-size: clamp(32px, 6vw, 56px); letter-spacing: -0.04em; line-height: 1.05; color: var(--ink); text-wrap: pretty; overflow-wrap: break-word; hyphens: auto;"
      >
        {gettext("The board your people and your agents share.")}
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
        {gettext(
          "Stride is an AI-native work management system. Every surface is built so humans and agents can both work the board without one getting in the other's way. Here is what each piece looks like."
        )}
      </p>

      <img
        src={~p"/images/marketing/product-hero.png"}
        alt={
          gettext(
            "Stride kanban board showing the Backlog, Ready, Doing, Review, and Done columns"
          )
        }
        width="1222"
        height="700"
        fetchpriority="high"
        class="mt-12 block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
        style="border: 1px solid var(--line);"
      />
    </header>

    <section id="plan" class="mb-24" aria-labelledby="plan-heading">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
        <span class="ucase">{gettext("01 · Plan")}</span>
        <h2
          id="plan-heading"
          class="font-semibold mt-3 mb-4"
          style="font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 40px); letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.1; color: var(--ink); text-wrap: pretty; overflow-wrap: break-word; hyphens: auto;"
        >
          {gettext("Plan at the level you think at")}
        </h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
          {gettext(
            "See every board at a glance, choose the flow your work follows, and break big outcomes into goals that agents and people can pick up."
          )}
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14" data-showcase-item>
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--ink);">
            {gettext("All your boards at a glance")}
          </h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {gettext(
              "Each board card shows its tasks in To Do, Doing, Review and Done, its throughput over the last 14 days and when work last moved. The page refreshes every 30 seconds."
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
        <img
          src={~p"/images/marketing/product-boards.png"}
          alt={gettext("Stride boards view")}
          width="1212"
          height="400"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--line);"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16" data-showcase-item>
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--ink);">
            {gettext("A fixed flow for agents, or columns of your own")}
          </h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {gettext(
              "AI-optimized boards use five fixed columns, Backlog, Ready, Doing, Review and Done, so people and agents follow one protocol: people specify in Backlog, agents pull from Ready, and people review in Review. On a custom board you add, rename, reorder and remove your own columns and set WIP limits. Cards move live as work happens."
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
        <img
          src={~p"/images/marketing/product-board.png"}
          alt={
            gettext(
              "The Ready, Doing and Review columns of a Stride board, with cards waiting, in progress and in review"
            )
          }
          width="860"
          height="292"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--line);"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16" data-showcase-item>
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--ink);">
            {gettext("Goals that track their own progress")}
          </h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {gettext(
              "A goal groups related tasks and shows how many are complete, with a progress bar split by status. Break work down from the top and claim it from the bottom. Reassigning a goal moves every unfinished task under it to the new assignee in one step."
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
        <img
          src={~p"/images/marketing/product-goal.png"}
          alt={
            gettext("Stride goal view with the segmented progress bar and child tasks beneath it")
          }
          width="1218"
          height="622"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--line);"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="build" class="mb-24" aria-labelledby="build-heading">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
        <span class="ucase">{gettext("02 · Build")}</span>
        <h2
          id="build-heading"
          class="font-semibold mt-3 mb-4"
          style="font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 40px); letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.1; color: var(--ink); text-wrap: pretty; overflow-wrap: break-word; hyphens: auto;"
        >
          {gettext("Structured schema, not free-text")}
        </h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
          {gettext(
            "A task carries more than a title: why, what, acceptance criteria, testing strategy, security considerations, pitfalls to avoid and observability. Agents claim with enough context to work without round-trips, and people review against criteria they wrote."
          )}
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14" data-showcase-item>
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--ink);">
            {gettext("Everything an agent needs, in one task")}
          </h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {gettext(
              "Open a task to see why it matters, what to build, where in the code it lives, its acceptance criteria and the key files to touch, next to its status, priority, complexity and whether it needs review."
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
        <img
          src={~p"/images/marketing/product-task-detail.png"}
          alt={
            gettext(
              "A Stride task showing its why, what, where, acceptance criteria and key files"
            )
          }
          width="990"
          height="765"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--line);"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16" data-showcase-item>
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--ink);">
            {gettext("Tests, security and pitfalls, spelled out")}
          </h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {gettext(
              "A task can also carry verification steps, a behaviour/test matrix that names the test for each behaviour, pitfalls to avoid, security considerations, a testing strategy and the telemetry and logging it needs, so finished work is checked against what was asked."
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
        <img
          src={~p"/images/marketing/product-task-schema.png"}
          alt={
            gettext(
              "A Stride task's verification steps, behaviour/test matrix, pitfalls and security considerations"
            )
          }
          width="724"
          height="625"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--line);"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="review" class="mb-24" aria-labelledby="review-heading">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
        <span class="ucase">{gettext("03 · Review")}</span>
        <h2
          id="review-heading"
          class="font-semibold mt-3 mb-4"
          style="font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 40px); letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.1; color: var(--ink); text-wrap: pretty; overflow-wrap: break-word; hyphens: auto;"
        >
          {gettext("Approve with the evidence in front of you")}
        </h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
          {gettext(
            "Finished work waits in one review queue. Read the reviewer's report, check the diff, then approve it or send it back with notes."
          )}
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14" data-showcase-item>
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--ink);">
            {gettext("Review queue")}
          </h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {gettext(
              "The queue lists the tasks waiting for your review across your boards, oldest first, with how long each has waited. Select one to see its completion summary, the reviewer's report with issues by severity, and how it did on acceptance criteria, testing strategy, patterns and pitfalls."
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
        <img
          src={~p"/images/marketing/product-review-queue.png"}
          alt={
            gettext(
              "The Stride review queue with a selected task's reviewer report and acceptance checks"
            )
          }
          width="1206"
          height="738"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--line);"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16" data-showcase-item>
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--ink);">
            {gettext("The checks and the diff, file by file")}
          </h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {gettext(
              "See the reviewer's evidence for each acceptance criterion, the review checks, and every file the agent changed with its diff inline. Approve to move the task to Done, or request changes with notes the agent picks up."
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
        <img
          src={~p"/images/marketing/product-review-diff.png"}
          alt={
            gettext(
              "The review checks and changed files in the Stride review queue, with one file's diff open"
            )
          }
          width="846"
          height="722"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--line);"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <%!-- Operate theme (W2458): the Agents page, My Work, delivery targets,
    notifications, integrations and the MCP server. Every subsection is a
    [data-showcase-item] with an image or a code snippet and a guide link. --%>
    <section id="operate" class="mb-24" aria-labelledby="operate-heading">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
        <span class="ucase">{gettext("04 · Operate")}</span>
        <h2
          id="operate-heading"
          class="font-semibold mt-3 mb-4"
          style="font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 40px); letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.1; color: var(--ink); text-wrap: pretty; overflow-wrap: break-word; hyphens: auto;"
        >
          {gettext("Keep work moving once it starts")}
        </h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
          {gettext(
            "Watch every agent as it works, see what is yours across boards, plan toward dates and hear about what needs you, in Stride, by email, in Slack or Discord, or through your own tools."
          )}
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14" data-showcase-item>
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--ink);">
            {gettext("See what every agent is doing")}
          </h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {gettext(
              "The Agents page shows each agent on your boards as working, waiting for review or idle, with its completions today and over seven days, its success rate and claims, next to a live feed of claims, completions and reviews."
            )}
            {gettext(
              "When a goal under an at-risk delivery target stalls, the target's owner or the board's owner can reassign or reprioritize it from this page, with 8 seconds to undo."
            )}
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            <.link
              href={~p"/resources/watching-your-agents"}
              class="font-medium underline"
              style="color: var(--stride-orange-ink); text-underline-offset: 2px;"
            >
              {gettext("Read the guide: Watching your agents")}
            </.link>
          </p>
        </div>
        <img
          src={~p"/images/marketing/product-agent-activity.png"}
          alt={gettext("The Stride Agents page with the agent roster and the activity feed")}
          width="1206"
          height="640"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--line);"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16" data-showcase-item>
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--ink);">
            {gettext("Everything assigned to you, on one page")}
          </h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {gettext(
              "My Work lists the open tasks assigned to you on every board you belong to, one card per board, most urgent first: Critical, then High, Medium and Low. Click a task to open it on its board."
            )}
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            <.link
              href={~p"/resources/your-work-across-boards"}
              class="font-medium underline"
              style="color: var(--stride-orange-ink); text-underline-offset: 2px;"
            >
              {gettext("Read the guide: Your work across boards")}
            </.link>
          </p>
        </div>
        <img
          src={~p"/images/marketing/product-my-work.png"}
          alt={
            gettext(
              "The Stride My Work page with assigned tasks grouped by board, the most urgent first"
            )
          }
          width="1198"
          height="306"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--line);"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16" data-showcase-item>
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--ink);">
            {gettext("Plan toward a date across boards")}
          </h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {gettext(
              "A delivery target groups goals from any of your boards under one date. Stride estimates when the work will finish from how long tasks have been taking and marks the target On-track, At-risk, Missed or Complete, so you see a date at risk before it slips."
            )}
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            <.link
              href={~p"/resources/planning-with-targets"}
              class="font-medium underline"
              style="color: var(--stride-orange-ink); text-underline-offset: 2px;"
            >
              {gettext("Read the guide: Planning with targets")}
            </.link>
          </p>
        </div>
        <img
          src={~p"/images/marketing/product-target.png"}
          alt={
            gettext(
              "A Stride delivery target with its date, status, estimated finish, progress by column and its goal"
            )
          }
          width="1194"
          height="328"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--line);"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16" data-showcase-item>
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--ink);">
            {gettext("Told when work needs you")}
          </h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {gettext(
              "The bell counts your unread notifications: review requests and results, task assignments, released claims, mentions and more. For each event you choose in-app, email or both, and a weekly digest email on Mondays sums up the past week, skipping quiet weeks."
            )}
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            <.link
              href={~p"/resources/staying-informed-with-notifications"}
              class="font-medium underline"
              style="color: var(--stride-orange-ink); text-underline-offset: 2px;"
            >
              {gettext("Read the guide: Staying informed with notifications")}
            </.link>
          </p>
        </div>
        <img
          src={~p"/images/marketing/product-notifications.png"}
          alt={
            gettext(
              "The Stride notifications page with review requests, a released claim and a mention"
            )
          }
          width="1179"
          height="481"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--line);"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16" data-showcase-item>
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--ink);">
            {gettext("Send board events to Slack, Discord or your own service")}
          </h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {gettext(
              "A board's owner can send its task events, such as a task created, moved to Review or completed, to a Slack or Discord channel or to a webhook of their own. Generic webhooks are signed with HMAC-SHA256 in an X-Stride-Signature header, failed deliveries are retried, and each endpoint keeps a log of recent deliveries."
            )}
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            <.link
              href={~p"/resources/connecting-webhooks-slack-and-discord"}
              class="font-medium underline"
              style="color: var(--stride-orange-ink); text-underline-offset: 2px;"
            >
              {gettext("Read the guide: Connecting webhooks, Slack and Discord")}
            </.link>
          </p>
        </div>
        <img
          src={~p"/images/marketing/product-integrations.png"}
          alt={
            gettext(
              "A Stride generic webhook with its events and its recent deliveries, including a failed attempt"
            )
          }
          width="574"
          height="348"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--line);"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16" data-showcase-item>
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--ink);">
            {gettext("Let agents work through MCP")}
          </h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
            {gettext(
              "Stride's MCP server gives an agent the task loop as six tools: get the next task, claim it, read a task, list tasks, add a comment and complete the work. It takes the same API token as the REST API. Add it to Claude Code with your own address and token:"
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
        <pre
          tabindex="0"
          aria-label={gettext("Commands that add Stride's MCP server to Claude Code")}
          class="mx-auto max-w-3xl overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl p-5 text-left text-sm leading-relaxed"
          style="background: var(--surface-sunken); border: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--ink);"
        ><code class="font-mono">{mcp_snippet()}</code></pre>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-center">
          <.link
            href={~p"/resources/connecting-an-mcp-client"}
            class="font-medium underline"
            style="color: var(--stride-orange-ink); text-underline-offset: 2px;"
          >
            {gettext("Read the guide: Connecting an MCP client")}
          </.link>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <%!-- Measure theme (interim). W2459 extends this section with the metrics
    pages and adds a Govern theme (Organizations and admin) after it. --%>
    <section id="measure" class="mb-24" aria-labelledby="measure-heading">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-6">
        <span class="ucase">{gettext("05 · Measure")}</span>
        <h2
          id="measure-heading"
          class="font-semibold mt-3 mb-4"
          style="font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 40px); letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.1; color: var(--ink); text-wrap: pretty; overflow-wrap: break-word; hyphens: auto;"
        >
          {gettext("Know where work waits")}
        </h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
          {gettext(
            "Workspace metrics show median cycle time, median lead time, throughput and review wait time over 7, 14, 30 or 90 days, for all your boards or just the ones you pick, with cumulative flow and a leaderboard of the agents and people finishing the work."
          )}
        </p>
      </div>
      <img
        src={~p"/images/marketing/product-metrics.png"}
        alt={
          gettext(
            "Stride workspace metrics with cycle time, lead time, throughput, review wait time and a leaderboard of agents and people"
          )
        }
        width="1232"
        height="782"
        loading="lazy"
        class="block mx-auto max-w-full h-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"
        style="border: 1px solid var(--line);"
      />
    </section>

    <%!-- Govern theme slot: W2459 adds Organizations and the admin console here. --%>

    <section class="bg-base-100 rounded-2xl border border-base-300 p-8 md:p-12 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-base-content mb-4">
        {gettext("Ready to see it run?")}
      </h2>
      <p class="mb-6 max-w-xl mx-auto" style="color: var(--ink-2);">
        {gettext("Free for you and your teams.")}
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 justify-center">
        <.link
          href={~p"/users/register"}
          class="px-6 py-3 rounded-lg bg-primary text-primary-content font-semibold hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity"
        >
          {gettext("Start now")}
        </.link>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</main>
